+# Skip controls and seek fix — 1.1.3
+
+Built from the uploaded stremio-webos(2).zip. Existing customizations are retained.
+
+Changes:
+- Down (key codes 40 and 29461) on Skip Intro/Outro opens player controls and focuses the timeline without pausing or seeking.
+- Skip is offered again after controls hide if playback is still inside the segment. Playback updates do not steal focus back while controls are open.
+- Existing remote OK and pointer skipping are preserved. While a skip is pending, playback updates cannot recreate the button; controls receive focus. Playback reaching the target confirms success. After eight seconds without reaching the target, a notice appears and controls remain accessible; Skip becomes retryable when controls hide.
+- An intro ends at its end timestamp, rather than including that timestamp and reappearing there.
+- WebOsVideo retains the latest seek while metadata is unavailable, retries a thrown native seek on loadeddata/canplay, and clears pending requests on unload/new stream. A pending user seek takes priority over the startup resume timestamp.
+- Runtime/chunk URLs change so the modified player code is fetched instead of an older cached chunk.
+- App and service versions are 1.1.3. App/service IDs are unchanged.
+
+Validation:
+- The unmodified upload fails the Down focus regression test; the patched player passes.
+- The original WebOsVideo loses a seek requested before metadata. The patched module passes readiness, latest-request, transient-exception, paused-state, and unload tests.
+- Delayed and failed seek scenarios verify that repeated OK cannot get trapped on a recreated Skip button, a failed seek gives feedback, and a later retry works.
+- Player tests execute the shipped Solid components and spatial navigation in Chromium with mocked playback/API state. Native-video tests execute the shipped WebOsVideo module with a native-video double.
+- These tests cannot verify LG decoding, stream seekability, timestamp accuracy, or native-player failures that silently ignore a seek. Those require a TV test.
+
+Run tests:
+    node tests/webos-seek.cjs
+    node tests/skip-intro.cjs
+
+The browser test requires Playwright and Chromium. BROWSER_EXECUTABLE can select an installed Chromium binary.
+
+Install the supplied IPK using your configured ares device, for example:
+    ares-install --device tv io.strem.webos_1.1.3_all.ipk
+
+Close Stremio before installation, then reopen it. Check Down, then OK after the controls hide, on a stream where skipping previously failed. Check both the beginning of playback and an already-running stream.
+
+WSL project:
+The updated ZIP contains the patched project. The patch at patches/skip-controls-and-seek.patch describes changes against the uploaded source, including tests. For a project still matching the upload:
+    git apply --check patches/skip-controls-and-seek.patch
+    git apply patches/skip-controls-and-seek.patch
+    make package
+Do not apply this patch to the already-patched files in the updated ZIP. If your WSL files have changed since the upload, use the check to detect conflicts before applying anything. build.sh is unchanged; it targets a different directory layout. Use the Makefile's package target.
+
+Timeline segment data:
+This player's available data path is introOutro.intro.from/to and introOutro.outro. It does not currently render coloured segment markers or handle a distinct recap field. No guessed recap timestamps or colours were added.
